      --  a bit in this range will cause the corresponding output to be set
      --  high. A logic zero written to a bit in this range shall cause the
      --  corresponding output to be forced low. Any unused bits will be read
      --  as logic zero. Writing to any unused bits in this range will have no
      --  functional effect.
